# Backend Python conventions

## Module layering

```
analysis/*       → pure, no DB / network. Used by signals.py + index_signals.py.
data/*           → yfinance + CSV cache + SQLAlchemy DAOs.
core/*           → orchestration (pipeline, index_pipeline, scheduler, universe).
ai/*             → LLM providers (template / ollama / openai).
api/*            → FastAPI routers — thin, delegate to core/* services.
live_analysis/*  → Upstox-backed observation + decision tracking (read-only).
```

API routers must NOT call yfinance directly; route via `core/pipeline.py`,
`core/index_pipeline.py`, or `data/fetcher.py`.

The paper-trading bot layers (`app/paper/` and `app/paper_index/`) have
been removed from this codebase. Do not reintroduce them.

## Indicators & analysis

Indicators are **hand-rolled** in `analysis/indicators.py` for deterministic
test output. Do not call `pandas-ta` from new code; extend the existing
function set if you need a new indicator and add a unit test.

## ORM & schemas

- New tables → add to `models/orm.py`, `models/index_orm.py`, or
  `models/live_analysis_orm.py` using the shared `Base`. `init_db()` calls
  `Base.metadata.create_all` and imports each side-effect module so new
  tables are picked up automatically.
- Pydantic v2: use `model_config = ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)` for
  ORM → JSON.
- Enum-like fields stay as `str` columns; whitelist values in the schema.

## Concurrency / scheduling

- `yf_client.pace()` enforces app-layer pacing for yfinance — keep it.
- `core/scheduler.py` uses APScheduler. Jobs must be idempotent because
  `/admin/refresh-async` can run them on demand too. The scheduler runs
  ONLY data refreshes + verification — no position-management jobs.

## Style

- Type hints on all public functions.
- Prefer `dataclass(frozen=True)` for value objects.
- Don't catch `Exception` without re-raising or logging structured context.
